{"name":"Hellbound","hex":"#710101","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hellbound","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bound for Hell; damned."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hellbound"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hellbound (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Hellbound (Korean: 지옥) is a South Korean supernatural dark fantasy thriller horror television series written and directed by Yeon Sang-ho with Choi Gyu-seok, based on their own webtoon of the same name. Set in the then future year of 2022, supernatural beings suddenly appear out of nowhere to condemn people to Hell. The series stars an ensemble cast including Yoo Ah-in, Kim Hyun-joo, Park Jeong-min, Won Jin-ah, Yang Ik-june, Kim Do-yoon, Kim Shin-rok, Ryu Kyung-soo, Lee Re, Kim Sung-cheol, Im Seong-jae, Lee Dong-hee, Hong Eui-jun, and Cho Dong-in"}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Hellbound_%28TV_series%29_title_card.png/330px-Hellbound_%28TV_series%29_title_card.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hellbound_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q100934044"},{"title":"Hellbound (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Hellbound \", or simply \"Hellbound\", is a song written and recorded by American rappers Eminem, J-Black and Masta Ace for the Yosumi Records compilation album Game Over (2000). The song was produced by DJ Rob and is a remix of Eminem's verse on \"Hustlers & Hardcore\" from Domingo's 1999 album Behind the Doors of the 13th Floor."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/44/Eminem%2C_Masta_Ace_%26_J-Black_-_Hellbound_%28H_%26_H_Remix%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hellbound_(song)","wikidata":"Q16842801"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Hellbound_%28TV_series%29_title_card.png/500px-Hellbound_%28TV_series%29_title_card.p